{"id":"7d19954c-4ebb-4ec2-b3cb-b1437426e63a","object":"chat.completion","created":1793336547,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Reading the remaining logger/format details I need before editing (already registered; using the delivered blocks above). Now adding the config factory and item in `environ.py`.\n\n```python\np = \"deepinfer/environ.py\"\nh = \"fe2c531989c419f0b51b169a07f5ed826dcec7f95c0c5bc3a351805923c4f218\"\nold1 = '''    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n'''\nnew1 = '''    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def bounded_int_or_none(*, minimum: int) -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        \"\"\"未设置时为 None；设置时必须是能解析且不小于 minimum 的整数。\"\"\"\n\n        def _init(v: str | None) -> int | None:\n            if v is None:\n                return None\n            try:\n                value = int(v)\n            except (TypeError, ValueError) as e:\n                raise ValueError(f\"must be an integer >= {minimum}, got {v!r}\") from e\n            if value < minimum:\n                raise ValueError(f\"must be >= {minimum}, got {value}\")\n            return value\n\n        return EnvVar(_init)\n'''\nr = replace_text(p, old1, new1, h)\nprint(r)\nprint(run_command([\"python\",\"-c\",\"print(1)\"], \".\")[\"rc\"])\n```","reasoning_content":"The baseline was already done. All three files read in full (registered). Mechanisms exposed. Now I need to implement changes.\n\nLet me recall the environ.py details: I have EnvVar class with factory methods, envs class with \"Logging\" section, rearm/rearm_all.\n\nNeed to add DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS: int or None, >= 32, ValueError containing variable name.\n\nThe descriptor wraps exceptions with f\"{self.name}: {e}\" — that already includes the name. So raising