atches spec.\n\nIf budget < 15? Budget >= 32 so fine.\n\nCondition: if len(message) <= budget: unchanged.\n\nNow the config reading in _setup_logger: `from deepinfer.environ import envs` — check for circular import? logger imports environ; environ imports os, threading only. Fine. But logger.py's _setup_logger() is called at module import. environment import fine.\n\nBut wait — environ module imports nothing from logger, so no cycle.\n\nAlso there might be existing import of environ in logger.py? Not in the shown code. I'll add local import inside _setup_logger to be safe (avoid import-time issues).\n\nActually careful: import errors — importing environ at logger import time might trigger os.getenv reading of all? No, descriptors lazily read.\n\nNow setup: \n```python\n    fmt = NewLineFormatter(\n        _FORMAT,\n        datefmt=_DATE_FORMAT,\n        use_color=sys.stdout.isatty(),\n        max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS,\n    )\n```\nRepeated init doesn't re-add handler (already guarded). If env value invalid, raises ValueError at import of logger — acceptable.\n\nHmm but careful: _setup_logger is called at import; if DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS invalid, import fails. Tests likely call _setup_logger with env set. Fine.\n\nStats logger: in _log_worker, `logger.info(m)` → `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nWait: but keep_full_message must be exactly True → we pass Python True. Good.\n\nAlso there's the queue.put of msgs — unchanged.\n\nNow let me check logger.py lines 33-68 fully, plus we have format method. Need to check if there's anything after format like a `class` end. We have the full formatter (lines 33-68). Good.\n\nLet me now write edits. First environ.py: add factory method in EnvVar after int_or_none, and config entry in Logging section.\n\nI need exact current text. From evidence: environ lines 31-94 show the class. The changes:\n\n1) After `int_or_none` static method add new factory. Old text:\n```\n    @staticmethod\n    def int_or_none() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(lambda v: int(v) if v is not None else None)\n```\nReplace with same + new method.\n\n2) In Logging section:\n```\n    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n```\nadd `DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.positive_int_or_none(minimum=32)` — name it `int_or_none_at_least`.\n\nLet me do the edits now. I'll write replaced text carefully.\n\nAlso should the docstring mention semantics? Add a docstring line.\n\nLet's implement.\n\nFor logger.py, I need `import copy`. Add to imports.\n\nThen formatter __init__ signature and validation, plus helper _truncate, and format override.\n\nFull new formatter code:\n\n```python\n_OMITTED_MARKER = \"...<omitted>...\"\n\n\nclass NewLineFormatter(logging.Formatter):\n    \"\"\"...\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        fmt: str,\n        datefmt: str | None = None,\n        high_precision: bool = False,\n        use_color: bool = False,\n        *,\n        max_message_chars: int | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(fmt, datefmt)\n        if max_message_chars is not None:\n            if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int):\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be an int >= 32 or None, got {max_message_chars!r}\")\n            if max_message_chars < 32:\n                raise ValueError(f\"max_message_chars must be >= 32, got {max_message_chars}\")\n        self.high_precision = high_precision\n        self.use_color = use_color\n        self.max_message_chars = max_message_chars\n```\n\nWait requirement 1: \"其他值须为大于等于32的整数，布尔值不算整数，否则抛出 ValueError\". Yes.\n\nHmm: should I coerce non-int? No, raise.\n\nTruncate method:\n\n```python\n    def _truncate_message(self, message: str) -> str:\n        budget = self.max_message_chars\n        if budget is None or len(message) <= budget:\n            return message\n        remaining = budget - len(_OMITTED_MARKER)\n        if remaining <= 0:\n            return _OMITTED_MARKER[:budget]\n        head = (remaining + 1) // 2\n        tail = remaining - head\n        return message[:head] + _OMITTED_MARKER + (message[len(message) - tail:] if tail > 0 else \"\")\n```\n\nformat:\n\n```python\n    def format(self, record: logging.LogRecord) -> str:\n        if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", None) is not True:\n            full_message = record.getMessage()\n            if len(full_message) > self.max_message_chars:\n                record = copy.copy(record)\n                record.msg = self._truncate_message(full_message)\n                record.args = None\n        msg = super().format(record)\n        ...\n```\n\nNote record.getMessage() when msg is not a string and no args: getMessage does `msg = str(self.msg)`. Fine.\n\nCareful with copy.copy on LogRecord: shallow copy copies __dict__ — ok.\n\nNow the `format` of copy uses record.message computed by super().format. Good.\n\nLet me write the edits."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10117,"completion_tokens":2679,"total_tokens":12796,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4096},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2319},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4096,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":6021},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}